From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:00:23 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op world hooks: game events and wrapped game functions to
 the module

One hook layer for co-op on Hookshot (hos_coop_world.h, host/coop_world.c):
- events after one instruction: hos_coop_world_event -> the module's
  hos_coop_world. First one: the AI pause counter start (main+0x5e6778,
  nx2/coop_platform_lift.py) goes to the module as
  HOS_COOP_WORLD_COUNTER_START instead of into a ring in the game's heap,
  so host/coop_platform_ring.c, the game malloc and the ring pointer at
  main+0x3c46780 are not used any more.
- wrapped game functions: Lifter.wraps (a64_lift.py, sent to the emit
  workers through chunks.py EMIT_TABLES) makes every call of f_<entry>,
  and the indirect table, reach hos_coop_w_<entry> in a64_hooks.c, which
  calls hos_coop_wrap before and after the unchanged f_<entry>, to the
  module's hos_coop_wrap with the registers. nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
  lists them (build id and words checked, never one Hookshot hooks or
  edits by name). First one: the flag applier at main+0xb99980.
The exports are kept once the module answers HOS_COOP_WORLD_HELLO.
